WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:02.340
Instructor: So let's now try making a pull request.

00:02.340 --> 00:04.080
We'll use the same repository,

00:04.080 --> 00:07.560
the feature-branch-workflow for Colt

00:07.560 --> 00:09.630
and our chicken, Stevie.

00:09.630 --> 00:11.190
So we have this nav bar branch

00:11.190 --> 00:13.170
that Stevie already pushed up, right?

00:13.170 --> 00:15.360
We can see nav bar right there.

00:15.360 --> 00:16.920
We also have the pricing table branch,

00:16.920 --> 00:18.360
but that's already been merged in.

00:18.360 --> 00:20.490
We didn't use a pull request to do that.

00:20.490 --> 00:23.220
I'm currently working as Stevie

00:23.220 --> 00:25.650
and if we take a closer look at the nav bar branch,

00:25.650 --> 00:28.590
there's this button here, pull request.

00:28.590 --> 00:33.513
So first we can do a comparison between nav bar and main.

00:35.010 --> 00:38.370
Now it assumes that I want to compare with main

00:38.370 --> 00:40.140
because that's a default branch,

00:40.140 --> 00:42.090
but I could make a pull request

00:42.090 --> 00:44.130
to some other branch if I needed to,

00:44.130 --> 00:46.380
I could make a pull request to pricing table.

00:46.380 --> 00:48.240
Just not that common.

00:48.240 --> 00:50.940
So it tells me, all right, here's your comparison.

00:50.940 --> 00:51.773
Good news,

00:51.773 --> 00:55.020
we're able to automatically merge your branch,

00:55.020 --> 00:57.720
nav bar into main if we get to that point.

00:57.720 --> 01:01.410
So it's not going to merge without me clicking merge.

01:01.410 --> 01:05.460
Creating the pull request simply requests that merging.

01:05.460 --> 01:08.520
So we can see there's just two commits, right?

01:08.520 --> 01:12.330
We have the broken nav bar, the nav bar fix,

01:12.330 --> 01:13.290
here's the diff.

01:13.290 --> 01:15.420
We can see all the stuff that I added in,

01:15.420 --> 01:16.950
or Stevie added in.

01:16.950 --> 01:19.890
Anyway, if I decide I wanna make this poll request,

01:19.890 --> 01:22.500
I'll click that button, create poll request,

01:22.500 --> 01:23.910
and then I can put some title in here.

01:23.910 --> 01:26.370
It's just using the the name of the branch.

01:26.370 --> 01:31.370
So how about add in bootstrap nav bar?

01:31.590 --> 01:33.690
Okay, leave a comment.

01:33.690 --> 01:35.340
This is my comment.

01:35.340 --> 01:39.480
I can mention people, like I'll mention Colt.

01:39.480 --> 01:41.013
Please take a look.

01:41.850 --> 01:44.910
So that will actually mention him as a user.

01:44.910 --> 01:48.360
You know, I can have bold text, I can put code in here,

01:48.360 --> 01:49.920
I can do all sorts of stuff,

01:49.920 --> 01:51.960
different formatting and formatted information

01:51.960 --> 01:53.850
but I'm just gonna keep it simple.

01:53.850 --> 01:55.290
So add in boot strap nav bar.

01:55.290 --> 01:57.540
This is my comment at Colt, please take a look.

01:57.540 --> 01:59.430
Here we go, create pull request.

01:59.430 --> 02:02.223
So from my nav bar branch to the main branch.

02:04.470 --> 02:06.240
Alright, so here's the PR.

02:06.240 --> 02:09.120
You can see under PR's or pull requests, we have one,

02:09.120 --> 02:10.500
it's open.

02:10.500 --> 02:13.920
It was created by Stevie Chicks a couple seconds ago

02:13.920 --> 02:17.760
and we can also see the way that this repo is set up,

02:17.760 --> 02:19.560
Stevie can just merge it in.

02:19.560 --> 02:22.980
That probably is not the approach that we want to take.

02:22.980 --> 02:24.570
There are ways to restrict

02:24.570 --> 02:27.240
who can merge branches and organizations,

02:27.240 --> 02:28.950
or who can merge PR's,

02:28.950 --> 02:31.080
but for now anybody can merge it in.

02:31.080 --> 02:32.430
So Stevie could make that PR

02:32.430 --> 02:34.770
and then also just turn around and click merge,

02:34.770 --> 02:36.480
but I'm not gonna do that.

02:36.480 --> 02:39.870
Let's go switch over as Colt.

02:39.870 --> 02:43.330
So we'll refresh the page on Colt's computer

02:44.910 --> 02:47.190
and then we have this PR showing up.

02:47.190 --> 02:49.800
I also got a notification up here.

02:49.800 --> 02:52.470
I dismissed it when I wasn't recording unfortunately,

02:52.470 --> 02:54.300
but I got a notification for

02:54.300 --> 02:57.030
the fact that I was mentioned in this poll request.

02:57.030 --> 02:59.640
So I can respond to Stevie, right?

02:59.640 --> 03:04.050
I can decide one, I can merge it right now if I want to.

03:04.050 --> 03:05.400
I can close it and just say

03:05.400 --> 03:07.320
this poll request is going nowhere.

03:07.320 --> 03:09.630
We're not adding this in to the main branch.

03:09.630 --> 03:13.110
Or I can leave some comments like, you know,

03:13.110 --> 03:15.180
looks good or looks bad.

03:15.180 --> 03:17.550
Could you fix this or add this?

03:17.550 --> 03:19.080
Can you make this change?

03:19.080 --> 03:22.260
And changes can be added to a poll request

03:22.260 --> 03:25.350
after the poll request is originally created.

03:25.350 --> 03:27.540
We can continue to, like in this example,

03:27.540 --> 03:30.420
Stevie could continue to to add to the nav bar branch

03:30.420 --> 03:32.490
and respond to feedback,

03:32.490 --> 03:36.120
but for this demo, I'll do something like, looks good.

03:36.120 --> 03:40.050
Whoops, didn't mean to do caps but merging now.

03:40.050 --> 03:41.820
All right, so I'll leave that comment.

03:41.820 --> 03:43.320
I won't close it.

03:43.320 --> 03:44.340
So I haven't done any,

03:44.340 --> 03:47.400
I haven't taken action, but now I'm going to.

03:47.400 --> 03:49.290
So not every poll request

03:49.290 --> 03:52.410
can be merged automatically on GitHub.

03:52.410 --> 03:55.830
Just like when we're doing merges locally with git,

03:55.830 --> 03:59.010
not every branch merge is a fast forward,

03:59.010 --> 04:01.650
or not every one can be done automatically

04:01.650 --> 04:04.230
without generating any sort of conflicts.

04:04.230 --> 04:06.510
So what I'm doing here by clicking this button

04:06.510 --> 04:08.010
is telling GitHub,

04:08.010 --> 04:10.170
alright go ahead and do the merge yourself.

04:10.170 --> 04:12.240
So then we're going to have some code

04:12.240 --> 04:14.040
that has been merged in on GitHub

04:14.040 --> 04:15.840
that we don't have locally.

04:15.840 --> 04:17.460
So the main branch is going to change.

04:17.460 --> 04:19.500
I'm gonna click, all right,

04:19.500 --> 04:21.960
do I wanna change the commit message?

04:21.960 --> 04:23.520
This is fine.

04:23.520 --> 04:24.693
Confirm merge.

04:25.770 --> 04:28.620
Successfully merged and close this poll request.

04:28.620 --> 04:31.260
The nav bar branch can now be safely deleted.

04:31.260 --> 04:33.003
So let's just delete it now.

04:34.680 --> 04:37.860
Okay, so now we have successfully completed

04:37.860 --> 04:39.780
one part of his workflow where

04:39.780 --> 04:43.950
we went from working on a feature branch, Stevie made it,

04:43.950 --> 04:46.860
and then Colt actually added a commit, he fixed a bug.

04:46.860 --> 04:49.080
We pushed that up to GitHub, we make a pull request.

04:49.080 --> 04:50.730
That pull request was merged in

04:50.730 --> 04:53.430
and now if we look at our index html,

04:53.430 --> 04:57.180
we have the nav bar showing up on our main branch.

04:57.180 --> 04:59.460
So now other developers, everyone on the team,

04:59.460 --> 05:01.920
needs to go and get the latest changes.

05:01.920 --> 05:02.850
So to do that,

05:02.850 --> 05:06.450
and we could fetch or we can just pull origin main.

05:06.450 --> 05:07.990
This is on Colt's machine

05:09.780 --> 05:13.798
and now we should have the nav bar showing up somewhere.

05:13.798 --> 05:14.910
There it is.

05:14.910 --> 05:18.270
We have all that nav bar work from the nav bar branch.

05:18.270 --> 05:20.460
Just take a look at it here.

05:20.460 --> 05:21.450
There we are.

05:21.450 --> 05:23.730
So it's not very nice looking,

05:23.730 --> 05:26.643
but that came from a branch that Stevie created

05:26.643 --> 05:28.320
and pushed up to GitHub.

05:28.320 --> 05:31.050
Then we made that PR and then Colt's accepted it,

05:31.050 --> 05:31.920
merged it in,

05:31.920 --> 05:34.440
and now individual users, collaborators

05:34.440 --> 05:36.870
need to pull down the new main branch

05:36.870 --> 05:39.690
and we could do the same thing on Stevie's side.

05:39.690 --> 05:42.240
So we can get rid of the nav bar branch.

05:42.240 --> 05:44.730
We'll switch to main first.

05:44.730 --> 05:46.560
We can remove nav bar.

05:46.560 --> 05:51.030
So we can do git branch -D nav bar to delete it.

05:51.030 --> 05:53.970
So now it's gone, locally and on GitHub,

05:53.970 --> 05:56.190
and now I can pull down the latest version of main.

05:56.190 --> 05:58.060
So git pull origin main

06:00.120 --> 06:04.320
and our local main branch is updated, we have the nav bar.

06:04.320 --> 06:06.630
I can just show it here.

06:06.630 --> 06:07.560
So there we go.

06:07.560 --> 06:09.240
We have the same end results.

06:09.240 --> 06:10.470
The same thing that we did

06:10.470 --> 06:13.860
to make this pricing table merged into the main branch,

06:13.860 --> 06:15.900
except we did it via a poll request,

06:15.900 --> 06:18.720
an intermediate step that is done on GitHub

06:18.720 --> 06:21.240
where we can have discussion and you know, debate

06:21.240 --> 06:22.980
as to whether something should be merged in

06:22.980 --> 06:25.383
and that's our first intro to PR's.
